---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
import LinkButton from '@/components/LinkButton.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Projects — Josiah Smith"
  description="Active research and open-source work — SAR foundation models, complex-valued deep learning, and Earth observation for good."
>
  <div class="projects container" data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="projects__head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Projects</p>
      <h1 class="projects__title">Active research &amp; open-source work</h1>
      <p class="projects__lead">
        Where the phase-aware, physics-first ideas get built and put to use — from Amazon
        deforestation monitoring to the complex-valued library underneath most of it.
      </p>
    </header>

    <article class="project">
      <div class="project__bar">
        <h2 class="project__name">GuacamayaSAR</h2>
        <span class="project__status">active · research</span>
      </div>
      <div class="prose project__body">
        <p>
          An open Sentinel-1 SAR companion to Microsoft AI for Good's Project Guacamaya, built to
          close the <strong>cloud-cover gap</strong> in optical Amazon deforestation monitoring. The Colombian
          Amazon is cloud-covered for roughly half the year; during those months optical alerts go quiet,
          and the operational SAR alert (Wageningen RADD) still misses real events.
        </p>
        <p>Two complementary branches feed a fused change-detection model:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Amplitude branch</strong> — OlmoEarth (AI2) as a frozen geospatial foundation backbone
            over Sentinel-1 RTC scenes from the Microsoft Planetary Computer STAC catalog.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Coherence branch</strong> — ASF HyP3 burst-InSAR pairs producing interferometric coherence
            and unwrapped phase, wired into a <code>torch.complex64</code> tensor. This phase-preserving,
            complex-valued head is the novel contribution: coherence collapses on disturbance independent
            of brightness.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Headline metric: <strong
            >recall on a curated set of 66 RADD-missed deforestation events</strong
          > over Florencia, Caquetá.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="project__links">
        <LinkButton href="https://github.com/josiahwsmith10/GuacamayaSAR">Repository →</LinkButton>
        <span class="project__note">Blog post forthcoming.</span>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="project">
      <div class="project__bar">
        <h2 class="project__name">NISAR L-band geo-FM gap</h2>
        <span class="project__status">write-up in progress</span>
      </div>
      <div class="prose project__body">
        <p>
          Every public geospatial foundation model was pretrained on <strong>C-band</strong>
          SAR. NISAR is <strong>L-band</strong> — it penetrates vegetation canopy and has fundamentally
          different scattering physics. The wedge: frozen C-band-pretrained FMs should <em>not</em> transfer
          zero-shot to L-band NISAR. This project quantifies the gap by class, then proposes a phase-aware,
          truly complex-valued adapter on a frozen FM — leaning into L-band's real advantage for biomass
          under canopy.
        </p>
        <p>
          NISAR began continuous global L-band collection in Aug 2025, with calibrated products
          arriving mid-2026 — a narrow window in which "first published geo-FM evaluation on NISAR"
          is still unclaimed.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="project__links">
        <LinkButton href="/blog/nisar-lband-fm-gap" variant="ghost">Read the draft →</LinkButton>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="project">
      <div class="project__bar">
        <h2 class="project__name">complextorch</h2>
        <span class="project__status">open-source · live on PyPI</span>
      </div>
      <div class="prose project__body">
        <p>
          A lightweight <strong>complex-valued neural network</strong> library built on PyTorch — and
          the open-source foundation under the phase-aware work above.
          <code>complextorch.nn.*</code> mirrors <code>torch.nn.*</code> name-for-name, so a real-valued
          model ports to complex-valued by changing the import, running on PyTorch's native <code
            >cfloat</code
          > kernels.
        </p>
        <p>
          Beyond drop-in <code>Conv</code> / <code>Linear</code> / attention layers it ships variance-correct
          complex initializers, RNN/LSTM and Transformer stacks, batch/layer/RMS/group norm, magnitude
          and spectral pooling, Type-A / Type-B activations, variational-dropout &amp; ARD sparsity, and
          a set of
          <strong>U(1)-equivariant / -invariant "co-domain symmetry" modules</strong>
          (SurReal, CDS) for data whose absolute phase is arbitrary — radar, MRI, comms. Python 3.10–3.12,
          100% line coverage enforced in CI.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="project__links">
        <LinkButton href="/blog/complextorch" variant="ghost">Write-up →</LinkButton>
        <LinkButton href="https://github.com/josiahwsmith10/complextorch">Repository →</LinkButton>
        <LinkButton href="https://josiahwsmith10.github.io/complextorch/latest/">Docs →</LinkButton>
        <LinkButton href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.07948">Paper →</LinkButton>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="project">
      <div class="project__bar">
        <h2 class="project__name">ideas-geospatial</h2>
        <span class="project__status">scoping</span>
      </div>
      <div class="prose project__body">
        <p>
          A working notebook of geospatial research ideas being scoped and pruned, including the
          NISAR L-band FM gap above, cross-sensor super-resolution, and an open ComSAR agent.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .projects {
    max-width: 52rem;
    padding-top: var(--sp-8);
  }
  .projects__title {
    font-size: var(--fs-2xl);
    margin-top: var(--sp-3);
  }
  .projects__lead {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin-top: var(--sp-4);
    max-width: 42rem;
  }

  .project {
    margin-top: var(--sp-8);
    padding-top: var(--sp-5);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
  }
  .project__bar {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--sp-4);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .project__name {
    font-size: var(--fs-xl);
  }
  .project__status {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-2xs);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--forest);
  }
  .project__body {
    margin-top: var(--sp-4);
  }
  .project__links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--sp-3);
    margin-top: var(--sp-5);
  }
  .project__note {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-2xs);
    color: var(--mist);
  }
</style>
